ur product settings at the credit agency.  More information: API for SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration  (Log on with your SAP ID to access this document.)\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-28\nValid as Of: 2024-02-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n\",1430\n244,\"--- Record 3361 ---\nComponent: Cloud Logging\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Updates\nDescription: Improve index template and index pattern for metric-otel-v1-* indices.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-29\nValid as Of: 2024-02-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3362 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Application Group Widget - Aligned Behavior\nDescription: Until now, the Application Group widget behaved differently when accessed from a workpage rather than through the Applications page. This behavior has been aligned and the widget behaves the same no matter where it is accessed from.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-22\nValid as Of: 2024-02-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3363 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Public Workspace: Role-Based Access for Non-Members\nDescription: Company administrators can define role-based access to workspaces for non-members. Workspace admins who are not company admins can view the settings but can't modify them.  To set this option, go to the Participation tab of the workspace settings, Non-Member Settings section, and in the Access Policy options choose Specific roles. Note that the roles you choose here must be assigned to users in the SAP BTP cockpit (Security  Users screen).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-22\nValid as Of: 2024-02-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3364 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: OpenID Connect\nDescription: Identity Authentication supports public clients for resource owner password credentials flow, JWT bearer flow, and token exchange flow. See Configure OpenID Connect Application for Resource Owner Password Credentials Flow, Configure OpenID Connect Application for JWT Bearer Flow, and Configure OpenID Connect Application for Token Exchange.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-28\nValid as Of: 2024-02-28\nVersion: 25719\n\n--- Record 3365 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Identity Authentication has been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-28\nValid as Of: 2024-02-28\nVersion: 25719\n\n--- Record 3366 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Subject Name Identifier\nDescription: The configuration of the Subject Name Identifier in the administration console for SAP Cloud Identity Services has been changed. Now, you can choose the primary attribute value from three sources: Identity Directory, Corporate Identity Provider, and Expression. They replace the Basic and Advanced configurations. See Configure the Subject Name Identifier Sent to the Application.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-28\nValid as Of: 2024-02-28\nVersion: 25719\n\n--- Record 3367 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Query parameter membersType in Proxy System SCIM API\nDescription: When using Identity Provisioning Proxy System SCIM API, you can now specify the membersType query parameter for groups. It controls the type of members (user or group) to be included in the response.  For more information, see Proxy Systems.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-20\nValid as Of: 2024-02-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3368 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Renamed System\nDescription: The Microsoft Azure Active Directory connector has been renamed to Microsoft Entra ID.  For more information, see: Microsoft Entra ID\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-20\nValid as Of: 2024-02-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3369 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Warning message in target systems\nDescription: A warning message informs you that it is recommended to configure ips.delete.threshold.users and ips.delete.threshold.groups properties in your target systems. These properties will prevent you from accidentally deleting a huge number of users and groups.  For more information, see List of Properties → ips.delete.threshold.users and ips.delete.threshold.groups.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-20\nValid as Of: 2024-02-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3370 ---\nComponent: SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New API available on SAP Business Accelerator Hub\nDescription: Use this API to receive information about companies or business partners from the credit agency, or change your product settings at the credit agency.  More information: API for SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration  (Log on with your SAP ID to access this document.)\n\",1430\n393,\"--- Record 1511 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Chart mode is available as part of the model library.  For more information, see Model Libra